{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>will revive us</b> — He will heal us, like וימרחו על השחין ויחי, until their restoration to life." "<b>And the meaning of 'two days'</b> — a near time." "<b>the third</b> — the opposite of 'all broken,' for then it hurts."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The quoted phrase is from 2 Kings 20:7/Isaiah 38:21; rendered literally it means 'and they applied [a plaster] upon the boil and he lived.' The sense of עד חיותם is uncertain: possibly 'until their recovery' or 'in accordance with their vitality.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:21.456610216Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}